Developed-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>



From 71816c82f6e8d0482e9f1027f1a17b4d6e821215 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:00:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: Add support for the VDPU382 variant (RK3528)

The RK3528 has a VDPU382 decoder, which is register compatible with
the VDPU381 found on the RK3588 for the H.264, HEVC and VP9 codecs, so
reuse the VDPU381 backends for it, with the following differences:

- the three decoder caches must be configured and cleared before each
  job, through a separate "cache" register region,
- the hardware only removes the H.264 emulation prevention bytes when
  asked to (strmd_zero_rm_en),
- the error auto reset is disabled and errors are recovered from the
  IRQ handler, by resetting the decoder together with its IOMMU (which
  also resets the decoder on RK3528) while an empty IOMMU domain is
  attached, optionally pulsing the CRU resets too,
- the watchdog resets the decoder the same way, instead of writing to a
  register that only exists on older variants,
- H.264 is limited to 8-bit 4:2:0 (High profile, level 5.1), HEVC to
  4:2:0 8/10-bit (Main and Main 10, level 5.1) and VP9 to profiles 0
  and 2, all up to 4096x2304.

VP9 is only available on the RK3528A.

This follows the approach of the VDPU382 support for the RK3562 by
retro98boy in the Armbian kernel, and the vendor MPP sources.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
